{"documentCount":56,"nextId":56,"documentIds":{"0":"api-reference/","1":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference","2":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-parsing","3":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-parsing-parsesakkoinput-str-resultrootnode","4":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-parsing-tokenizeinput-str-resultvectoken","5":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-typechecking","6":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-typechecking-checksourcesrc-str-resultreport","7":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-typechecking-checkastast-astnode-report","8":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-report-types","9":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-report-types-report","10":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-report-types-diagnostic","11":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-report-types-jsescape","12":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-ast-node-types","13":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-ast-node-types-rootnode-elementnode-inlinenode-listnode","14":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-ast-node-types-reactive-snippets","15":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-ast-node-types-declaration-types","16":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-re-exports","17":"/","18":"/#sakko","19":"/#sakko-quick-start","20":"/#sakko-quick-start-lexing-only","21":"/#sakko-what-you-get","22":"/#sakko-reactivity","23":"/#sakko-documentation","24":"language-reference/","25":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference","26":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-file-extension","27":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-syntax-overview","28":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-syntax-overview-root-blocks","29":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-syntax-overview-block-elements","30":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-syntax-overview-inline-elements","31":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-syntax-overview-void-elements","32":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-modifiers","33":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-modifiers-flags-boolean","34":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-modifiers-key-value-pairs","35":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-lists","36":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-lists-inline-siblings-with-semicolons","37":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-strings","38":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-comments","39":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-reactivity","40":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-reactivity-state","41":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-reactivity-derived-state","42":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-reactivity-effects","43":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-reactivity-event-handlers","44":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-reactivity-two-way-binding","45":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-reactivity-conditionals-if","46":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-reactivity-iteration-each","47":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-reactivity-reactive-classes","48":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-reactivity-interpolation","49":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-sahō-expression-language","50":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-sahō-expression-language-equality-is-always-strict","51":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-sahō-expression-language-unknown-and-as-assertions","52":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-sahō-expression-language-js-escape-hatch","53":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-sahō-expression-language-builtins","54":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-complete-example","55":"language-reference/#sakko-language-reference-ast-output"},"fieldIds":{"title":0,"headings":1,"text":2},"fieldLength":{"0":[2,34,299],"1":[4,3,1],"2":[4,1,1],"3":[8,6,1],"4":[7,5,1],"5":[4,1,1],"6":[8,6,1],"7":[7,5,1],"8":[5,2,1],"9":[4,1,1],"10":[4,1,1],"11":[4,1,1],"12":[6,3,1],"13":[7,4,1],"14":[5,2,1],"15":[5,2,1],"16":[5,2,1],"17":[2,10,193],"18":[3,1,1],"19":[5,2,1],"20":[5,2,1],"21":[6,3,1],"22":[4,1,1],"23":[3,1,1],"24":[3,61,382],"25":[4,3,1],"26":[6,2,1],"27":[6,2,1],"28":[6,2,1],"29":[6,2,1],"30":[6,2,1],"31":[6,2,1],"32":[5,1,1],"33":[7,3,1],"34":[7,3,1],"35":[5,1,1],"36":[8,4,1],"37":[5,1,1],"38":[5,1,1],"39":[5,1,1],"40":[5,1,1],"41":[6,2,1],"42":[5,1,1],"43":[6,2,1],"44":[7,3,1],"45":[7,3,1],"46":[7,3,1],"47":[6,2,1],"48":[5,1,1],"49":[7,3,1],"50":[8,4,1],"51":[8,4,1],"52":[7,3,1],"53":[5,1,1],"54":[6,2,1],"55":[6,2,1]},"averageFieldLength":[5.499999999999999,4.053571428571426,16.553571428571434],"storedFields":{"0":{"title":"API Reference","id":"api-reference/","text":"Sakko API Reference\nAll types below are re-exported from the sakko crate root.\n\nParsing\nparse_sakko(input: &amp;str) -&gt; Result&lt;RootNode&gt;\nParse a .sako source string into a document AST.\nuse sakko::parse_sakko;\n\nlet ast = parse_sakko(r#&quot;&lt;counter { text: &quot;Hello&quot; }&gt;&quot;#)?;\n// ast: RootNode { name: &quot;counter&quot;, children: [...], ... }\n\nThe returned RootNode contains:\n\nname: Cow&lt;str&gt; - component tag name\nmodifiers: Vec&lt;Modifier&gt; - flag/pair modifiers on the root\ndeclarations: Vec&lt;AtcodeDeclaration&gt; - reactive block declarations (@state, @derived, @effect, @if, @each, @class, @on, @bind)\nchildren: Vec&lt;AstNode&gt; - child elements, inlines, and lists\n\n\ntokenize(input: &amp;str) -&gt; Result&lt;Vec&lt;Token&gt;&gt;\nTokenize a source string. Useful for lexing-level tooling; the parser uses\nthis internally.\nuse sakko::tokenize;\n\nlet tokens = tokenize(&quot;button(accent): Save&quot;)?;\n// Token { kind: TokenKind::Ident, value: &quot;button&quot;, ... }\n\nToken kinds: Lt, Gt, Lbrace, Rbrace, Lparen, Rparen,\nLbracket, Rbracket, Colon, Semi, Comma, Ident, String,\nBacktickString, At, Equals, InterpStart, InterpEnd, Expr,\nDot, Plus, Minus, Star, Pipe, Ampersand, Bang, Question,\nPercent.\n\nTypechecking\ncheck_source(src: &amp;str) -&gt; Result&lt;Report&gt;\nParse and typecheck a .sako source string in one call. Returns a Report\ncontaining diagnostics and raw-JS escape records.\nuse sakko::check_source;\n\nlet report = check_source(r#&quot;&lt;counter { @state { count = 0 } }&gt;&quot;#)?;\nassert!(report.diagnostics.is_empty());\n\ncheck_ast(ast: &amp;AstNode) -&gt; Report\nTypecheck an already-parsed AST node. parse_sakko returns a RootNode, so\nwrap it as AstNode::Root before passing it here:\nuse sakko::{AstNode, check_ast, parse_sakko};\n\nlet root = parse_sakko(r#&quot;&lt;counter { @state { count = 0 } }&gt;&quot;#)?;\nlet report = check_ast(&amp;AstNode::Root(root));\nassert!(report.diagnostics.is_empty());\n\n\nReport types\nReport\npub struct Report {\n    pub diagnostics: Vec&lt;Diagnostic&gt;,\n    pub js_escapes: Vec&lt;JsEscape&gt;,\n}\n\nDiagnostic\npub struct Diagnostic {\n    pub severity: Severity,   // currently always Error\n    pub code: Code,           // stable code: SKT001..SKT015\n    pub span: Span,\n    pub snippet: String,\n    pub caret: String,\n    pub message: String,\n    pub suggestion: Option&lt;String&gt;,\n}\n\nimpl Diagnostic {\n    pub fn render(&amp;self) -&gt; String { /* formatted with source + caret */ }\n}\n\nDiagnostic codes:\n\n\n\nCode\nName\nDescription\n\n\n\n\nSKT001\nUnknownIdent\nUnknown identifier\n\n\nSKT002\nUnknownProp\nUnknown property\n\n\nSKT003\nNotCallable\nValue is not callable\n\n\nSKT004\nAssignMismatch\nType mismatch in assignment\n\n\nSKT005\nBadOperand\nInvalid operand for operator\n\n\nSKT006\nBadUnaryOperand\nInvalid operand for unary operator\n\n\nSKT007\nDuplicateDecl\nDuplicate state declaration\n\n\nSKT008\nBadBindTarget\n@bind must target a state variable\n\n\nSKT009\nBadEachSource\nMalformed @each source\n\n\nSKT010\nRenderedFunction\nFunction used where a value is rendered\n\n\nSKT011\nSnippetParse\nSaho parse error inside a snippet\n\n\nSKT012\nConstReassign\nCannot reassign @derived or constant\n\n\nSKT013\nUnknownUse\nUse of a value the checker cannot resolve\n\n\nSKT014\nImpossibleCast\nas cast between disjoint concrete types\n\n\nSKT015\nBadClassType\n@class expression must yield a string or array of strings\n\n\n\nJsEscape\nOne recorded js { ... } occurrence. Bodies are never typechecked.\npub struct JsEscape {\n    pub kind_label: String,\n    pub location: Option&lt;(u32, u32)&gt;,\n    pub span: Span,\n    pub body: String,\n}\n\n\nAST node types\nRootNode / ElementNode / InlineNode / ListNode\npub struct RootNode&lt;&#039;a&gt; {\n    pub name: Cow&lt;&#039;a, str&gt;,\n    pub modifiers: Vec&lt;Modifier&lt;&#039;a&gt;&gt;,\n    pub declarations: Vec&lt;AtcodeDeclaration&lt;&#039;a&gt;&gt;,\n    pub children: Vec&lt;AstNode&lt;&#039;a&gt;&gt;,\n}\n\npub struct ElementNode&lt;&#039;a&gt; {\n    pub name: Cow&lt;&#039;a, str&gt;,\n    pub modifiers: Vec&lt;Modifier&lt;&#039;a&gt;&gt;,\n    pub children: Vec&lt;AstNode&lt;&#039;a&gt;&gt;,\n}\n\npub struct InlineNode&lt;&#039;a&gt; {\n    pub name: Cow&lt;&#039;a, str&gt;,\n    pub modifiers: Vec&lt;Modifier&lt;&#039;a&gt;&gt;,\n    pub value: InlineValue&lt;&#039;a&gt;,\n}\n\npub struct ListNode&lt;&#039;a&gt; {\n    pub items: Vec&lt;AstNode&lt;&#039;a&gt;&gt;,\n}\n\npub enum AstNode&lt;&#039;a&gt; {\n    Root(RootNode&lt;&#039;a&gt;),\n    Element(ElementNode&lt;&#039;a&gt;),\n    Inline(InlineNode&lt;&#039;a&gt;),\n    List(ListNode&lt;&#039;a&gt;),\n}\n\nReactive snippets\nEvery reactive payload is parsed once at document-parse time into a typed\nSaho node; the typechecker walks the pre-built tree (no re-parse).\npub struct ExprSnippet&lt;&#039;a&gt; {\n    pub raw: Cow&lt;&#039;a, str&gt;,\n    pub parsed: Option&lt;Box&lt;saho::Node&gt;&gt;,\n    pub errors: Vec&lt;SnippetDiag&gt;,\n}\n\npub struct BlockSnippet&lt;&#039;a&gt; {\n    pub raw: Cow&lt;&#039;a, str&gt;,\n    pub parsed: Option&lt;Vec&lt;saho"},"1":{"title":"API Reference > Sakko API Reference","id":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference","text":""},"2":{"title":"API Reference > Parsing","id":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-parsing","text":""},"3":{"title":"API Reference > parse_sakko(input: &str) -> Result<RootNode>","id":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-parsing-parsesakkoinput-str-resultrootnode","text":""},"4":{"title":"API Reference > tokenize(input: &str) -> Result<Vec<Token>>","id":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-parsing-tokenizeinput-str-resultvectoken","text":""},"5":{"title":"API Reference > Typechecking","id":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-typechecking","text":""},"6":{"title":"API Reference > check_source(src: &str) -> Result<Report>","id":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-typechecking-checksourcesrc-str-resultreport","text":""},"7":{"title":"API Reference > check_ast(ast: &AstNode) -> Report","id":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-typechecking-checkastast-astnode-report","text":""},"8":{"title":"API Reference > Report types","id":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-report-types","text":""},"9":{"title":"API Reference > Report","id":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-report-types-report","text":""},"10":{"title":"API Reference > Diagnostic","id":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-report-types-diagnostic","text":""},"11":{"title":"API Reference > JsEscape","id":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-report-types-jsescape","text":""},"12":{"title":"API Reference > AST node types","id":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-ast-node-types","text":""},"13":{"title":"API Reference > RootNode / ElementNode / InlineNode / ListNode","id":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-ast-node-types-rootnode-elementnode-inlinenode-listnode","text":""},"14":{"title":"API Reference > Reactive snippets","id":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-ast-node-types-reactive-snippets","text":""},"15":{"title":"API Reference > Declaration types","id":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-ast-node-types-declaration-types","text":""},"16":{"title":"API Reference > Re-exports","id":"api-reference/#sakko-api-reference-re-exports","text":""},"17":{"title":"Sakko Documentation","id":"/","text":"Sakko\nSakko is a bracket-based markup language that compiles to component trees for reactive UI. It is the front end of the S-eco stack: a typed document language, a strict expression sub-language (Sahō), and a compile-time typechecker, all Rust, all AOT.\nQuick start\nuse sakko::{parse_sakko, check_source};\n\nfn main() {\n    // Parse a .sako source string into a typed AST\n    let ast = parse_sakko(r#&quot;&lt;counter { @state { count = 0 } }&gt;&quot;#)\n        .expect(&quot;parse failed&quot;);\n\n    // Typecheck the AST, which returns diagnostics + raw-JS escape records\n    let report = check_source(r#&quot;&lt;counter { @state { count = 0 } }&gt;&quot;#)\n        .expect(&quot;parse failed&quot;);\n\n    if report.diagnostics.is_empty() {\n        println!(&quot;Clean.&quot;);\n    } else {\n        for d in &amp;report.diagnostics {\n            eprintln!(&quot;{}&quot;, d.render());\n        }\n    }\n}\n\nLexing only\nuse sakko::tokenize;\n\nlet tokens = tokenize(&quot;button(accent): Save&quot;)?;\n// Vec&lt;Token&gt; with line/column tracking and interpolation splits\n\nWhat you get\n\n\n\nFeature\nDetails\n\n\n\n\nLexer\nTokenizer with line/column tracking and {expr} string-interpolation splits\n\n\nSahō parser\nPratt expression parser (strict JS subset): types, arrows, js{}, as assertions\n\n\nStructure parser\nRecursive-descent parser for &lt;name { ... }&gt; documents\n\n\nAST\nZero-copy via spans; serde on all token/AST types\n\n\nTypechecker\nInference pass with stable diagnostic codes SKT001-SKT015\n\n\nReactive IR\n@state, @derived, @effect, @on:event, @bind, @each, @if, @class\n\n\n\nReactivity\nSakko compiles to Sairin signals for reactive UI:\n&lt;counter {\n  @state { count = 0 }\n  button @on:click { count++ }: &quot;+&quot;\n  text: &quot;Count: {count}&quot;\n}&gt;\n\n\n\n\nAtcode\nDescription\n\n\n\n\n@state { }\nDeclare reactive state\n\n\n@effect { }\nSide effects that track dependencies\n\n\n@derived { }\nComputed values\n\n\n@on:event { }\nEvent handlers\n\n\n@bind=&quot;signal&quot;\nTwo-way input binding\n\n\n{expr}\nTemplate interpolation (backtick or double-quoted strings)\n\n\n@if\nConditional rendering inside handlers and effects\n\n\n@each\nList iteration\n\n\n@class=&quot;expr&quot;\nDynamic class string or array\n\n\n\nDocumentation\n\n\n\nPage\nDescription\n\n\n\n\nLanguage Reference\nFull Sakko syntax: blocks, modifiers, lists, reactivity\n\n\nAPI Reference\nPublic Rust API: parse_sakko, tokenize, check_source, types\n\n\n\n"},"18":{"title":"Sakko Documentation > Sakko","id":"/#sakko","text":""},"19":{"title":"Sakko Documentation > Quick start","id":"/#sakko-quick-start","text":""},"20":{"title":"Sakko Documentation > Lexing only","id":"/#sakko-quick-start-lexing-only","text":""},"21":{"title":"Sakko Documentation > What you get","id":"/#sakko-what-you-get","text":""},"22":{"title":"Sakko Documentation > Reactivity","id":"/#sakko-reactivity","text":""},"23":{"title":"Sakko Documentation > Documentation","id":"/#sakko-documentation","text":""},"24":{"title":"Sakko Language Reference","id":"language-reference/","text":"Sakko Language Reference\nSakko is a bracket-based markup language for describing UI trees. It compiles\nto Sairin component trees, which render through Sazami. The expression\nsub-language used inside reactive payloads is called Sahō (作法), which is a\nstrict, typechecked JavaScript subset.\n\nFile extension\nSakko files use the .sako extension.\n\nSyntax overview\nRoot blocks\nEvery .sako file has one root block wrapped in angle brackets:\n&lt;name {\n  ...children\n}&gt;\n\nThe parser also accepts a bare name { ... } without angle brackets, using the\ninternal sentinel name __sakko_wrapper__. Prefer explicit &lt;tagname { ... }&gt;\nsyntax to avoid internal names in your artifacts.\nExample:\n&lt;page {\n  card { text: Hello }\n}&gt;\n\nBlock elements\nBlock elements contain child elements inside curly braces:\nelement {\n  child1: value\n  child2 { ... }\n}\n\nInline elements\nInline elements have no children: just a name, optional modifiers, and a value:\nname: value\nname(modifiers): value\n\nVoid elements\nElements that need no value or children can stand alone:\ndivider;\nspacer(large);\n\nThese are parsed as inline elements with an empty value.\n\nModifiers\nModifiers are placed in parentheses after the element name.\nFlags (boolean)\nSpace-separated tokens:\nbutton(accent large bold): Save\ncard(curved): { ... }\ntext(dim small): Label\n\nKey-value pairs\nSome tokens take a following value. Values can be bare identifiers or quoted\nstrings:\ngrid(cols 3 gap large): [...]\ninput(placeholder &quot;Enter your name&quot; type &quot;email&quot;): &quot;&quot;\n\nThe parser recognizes keys such as cols, gap, radius, size, variant,\nlayout, placeholder, type, src, alt, icon, label, value,\nmin, max, step, name, heading, slot, active, open, message,\ntitle, disabled, checked, selected, removable, required,\nmultiple, for, direction, and responsive variants like md:cols.\n\nStrict validation: Unknown modifier flags are errors. Custom modifiers can\nbe added to the recognized set.\n\n\nLists\nLists group multiple sibling elements, with items separated by commas:\n&lt;grid(cols 3) {\n  card { text: One },\n  card { text: Two },\n  card { text: Three }\n}&gt;\n\nLists appear after a colon or directly:\nrow: [button: A, button: B]\nrow {button: A, button: B}\n\nInline siblings with semicolons\nUse semicolons to place multiple inline elements on one line:\n&lt;controls {\n  button: play; button: pause; badge(accent): LIVE\n}&gt;\n\n\nStrings\n\nBare words for simple values (no spaces): text: Hello\nQuoted strings for values with spaces or special characters: text: &quot;Hello World&quot;\nInterpolated strings in double quotes support {expr}:\n\ntext: &quot;Price = {price * qty}&quot;\n\nIn expression snippets (@state, @derived, etc.) both backtick\n(`Price = ${price}`) and double-quote (&quot;Price = {price}&quot;) forms\ninterpolate.\n\nComments\nSingle-line comments start with //:\n// This is a comment\n&lt;card {\n  // Comments work anywhere\n  text: Content // Inline comments too\n}&gt;\n\n\nReactivity\nSakko supports inline reactivity through atcode declarations. These compile to\nSairin signals for reactive UI.\nState\nDeclare reactive state with @state:\n&lt;counter {\n  @state {\n    count = 0\n    step = 1\n  }\n\n  text: &quot;Count: {count}&quot;\n}&gt;\n\n@state declares variables that can be read and written. Values are\ninitialized with Sahō expressions. Types may be annotated with as:\n@state {\n  count = 0\n  label = &quot;x&quot; as string\n}\n\nDerived state\nCompute derived values with @derived:\n&lt;app {\n  @state { items = [] }\n  @derived {\n    count = items.length\n    isEmpty = items.length == 0\n  }\n  text: &quot;{count} items&quot;\n}&gt;\n\nDerived values are computed (immutable); reassigning one is an error\n(SKT012).\nEffects\nRun side effects with @effect:\n&lt;app {\n  @state { count = 0 }\n\n  @effect {\n    console.log(&quot;Count changed:&quot;, count)\n    js { document.title = `Count: ${count}` }\n  }\n\n  button @on:click { count++ }: &quot;Increment&quot;\n}&gt;\n\ndocument/window are not in the global manifest. DOM access like\ndocument.title works only inside js { ... } escape blocks.\nEffects run when any referenced state changes.\nEvent handlers\nHandle DOM events with @on:event:\nbutton @on:click { count++ }: &quot;Click&quot;\ninput @on:input { value = e.target.value }: &quot;&quot;\n\nThe handler body is Sahō. The event parameter e has type unknown;\nnavigation and calls on unknown are free, and you may assert its shape with\nas.\nTwo-way binding\nBind input elements with @bind:\n&lt;input @bind=&quot;username&quot;: &quot;&quot;&gt;\n&lt;checkbox @bind=&quot;checked&quot;: &quot;&quot;&gt;\n&lt;select @bind=&quot;value&quot;: &quot;&quot;&gt;\n\nThe bound signal syncs automatically with the input value. @bind must ta